 "level_notes": {
  "1": "The final Microsoft specification (1.9.1, Word 2007) is no longer on microsoft.com; the RTF 1.5 specification mirrored by Biblioscape is the most complete open HTML copy and is used for deep links. Microsoft's Open Specifications still document the compressed-RTF and RTF-extensions protocols used in Exchange.",
  "0": "No reference implementation; Word is the de-facto definition. LibreOffice's rtftok, rtf.js and striprtf are open readers."
 },
